+# QQ Bot
+
+Indus Agent connects to QQ through the official QQ Bot API.
+
+## What you need
+
+A bot on the QQ open platform: its **App ID** and **client secret** (AppSecret).
+
+## Setting it up
+
+```bash
+indus gateway setup qqbot
+```
+
+or set `QQ_APP_ID` and `QQ_CLIENT_SECRET`, then `indus gateway start`. The gateway opens QQ's
+WebSocket gateway itself, so nothing has to be public.
+
+## How it behaves
+
+- Private (C2C) chats, group chats, guild channels and guild direct messages each work as
+  conversations; in groups and channels the bot answers when mentioned.
+- Replies are split at 4,000 characters.
diff --git a/docs/user/messaging/raft.md b/docs/user/messaging/raft.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..82eb826
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/user/messaging/raft.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# Raft
+
+Raft keeps the conversation itself and only tells an outside agent when something may be waiting.
+Indus Agent provides that agent's door: a small wake endpoint on your machine.
+
+## Setting it up
+
+1. Install the Raft command-line tool and sign in; set `RAFT_PROFILE` to the Raft profile to use.
+2. Start the gateway (`indus gateway start`). It listens on `127.0.0.1` and writes the wake address
+   and its token to `<profile home>/platforms/raft/bridge.json` (readable only by you).
+3. Run `raft agent bridge` with the address from that file.
+
+## How it behaves
+
+- Only requests from this machine with the bridge token are accepted.
+- A wake makes the agent fetch and answer what is waiting through the Raft tool.
