index 0000000..a644655
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/user/messaging/teams.md
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# Microsoft Teams
+
+Indus Agent works as a Teams bot through the Bot Framework.
+
+## What you need
+
+An Azure Bot registration (or a Teams app with a bot) with its **app (client) id**, a **client
+secret** and the **tenant id**. The bot's messaging endpoint must be a public HTTPS URL that
+reaches the gateway.
+
+## Setting it up
+
+```bash
+indus gateway setup teams
+```
+
+or set `TEAMS_CLIENT_ID`, `TEAMS_CLIENT_SECRET` and `TEAMS_TENANT_ID`. The gateway listens for the
+Bot Connector on port 3978, path `/api/messages`, on loopback unless you open it
+(`platforms.teams.webhook_public`); put it behind your HTTPS reverse proxy and set that URL as the
+bot's messaging endpoint.
+
+## How it behaves
+
+- Every request must carry a valid Bot Framework token, and replies only go to Microsoft's own
+  service addresses.
+- Personal chats, group chats and channel threads are separate conversations; in channels the bot
+  answers when mentioned.
+- Approvals and questions use Adaptive Cards.
+
+Microsoft Graph change notifications (for example for mail or meetings) are a separate receiver;
+see [API server and webhooks](api-and-webhooks.md#microsoft-graph-change-notifications).
diff --git a/docs/user/messaging/telegram.md b/docs/user/messaging/telegram.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..727a759
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/user/messaging/telegram.md
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# Telegram
+
+Indus Agent talks to Telegram as a bot, through the Bot API. No extra libraries are needed.
+
+## What you need
+
+A bot token. In Telegram, open a chat with **@BotFather**, send `/newbot`, choose a name and a
+username, and copy the token it gives you.
+
+## Setting it up
+
+```bash
+indus gateway setup telegram
+```
+
+or set `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` yourself (`indus config set TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN <token>`), then
+`indus gateway start`. Write to your bot; it answers with a pairing code that you approve with
+`indus pairing approve telegram <code>`. To skip pairing for yourself, put your numeric user id in
+`INDUS_TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USERS`.
+
+## How it behaves
+
+- The gateway fetches updates by long polling; nothing has to be reachable from the internet. A
+  webhook can be configured instead (it always needs its secret).
+- In groups the bot answers when mentioned or replied to; in forum groups each topic is its own
+  conversation and replies stay in their topic.
+- Replies are written into the message as they stream, and long ones are split at Telegram's
+  4,096-character limit.
+- Approvals and questions show as buttons. The bot's command menu lists the slash commands.
+- Photos, voice notes and documents you send are passed to the agent (voice notes are transcribed
+  when speech to text is set up).
diff --git a/docs/user/messaging/wecom.md b/docs/user/messaging/wecom.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7076a55
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/user/messaging/wecom.md
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+# WeCom
+
+Indus Agent supports two kinds of WeCom (WeChat Work) integration.
+
+| | Smart robot | Callback app |
+|---|---|---|
+| Platform name | `wecom` | `wecom_callback` |
+| Connection | one WebSocket opened by the gateway | WeCom calls the gateway's endpoint |
+| Credentials | `WECOM_BOT_ID`, `WECOM_SECRET` | `WECOM_CALLBACK_CORP_ID`, `WECOM_CALLBACK_CORP_SECRET`, `WECOM_CALLBACK_AGENT_ID`, `WECOM_CALLBACK_TOKEN`, `WECOM_CALLBACK_ENCODING_AES_KEY` |
+
+## Smart robot
+
+Create an intelligent robot in the WeCom admin console with the long connection API and copy its
+bot id and secret. Then `indus gateway setup wecom`, or set the two variables. WeCom allows one
+connection per robot: if a second gateway uses the same robot, the first one stops and says so.
+
+## Callback app
+
+Create a self-built application in the WeCom admin console, set its message receiving URL to the
+gateway's callback endpoint (published through your HTTPS reverse proxy), and copy the corp id,
+the app's secret and agent id, and the token and encoding AES key you set there. Then
+`indus gateway setup wecom_callback`. Messages are verified and decrypted with those keys.
diff --git a/docs/user/messaging/weixin.md b/docs/user/messaging/weixin.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..270fd00
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/user/messaging/weixin.md
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+# Weixin
+
+Indus Agent can answer from a personal WeChat (Weixin) account through Tencent's iLink bot
+interface.
+
+## What you need
+
+An iLink bot **token** and the **account id** it belongs to.
+
+## Setting it up
+
+```bash
+indus gateway setup weixin
+```
+
+or set `WEIXIN_TOKEN` and `WEIXIN_ACCOUNT_ID`, then `indus gateway start`.
+
+## How it behaves
+
+- Private chats are conversations. Group messages are kept only when the group policy allows them
+  (`open`, or an allow-list naming the group); naming the bot in a group addresses it.
+- The gateway resumes from where it left off after a restart, so messages are neither lost nor
+  answered twice.
+- Media are encrypted the way iLink expects.
diff --git a/docs/user/messaging/whatsapp.md b/docs/user/messaging/whatsapp.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..63dac43
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/user/messaging/whatsapp.md
@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+# WhatsApp
+
+There are two ways to connect WhatsApp, for two kinds of account.
+
+| | WhatsApp Business (Cloud API) | WhatsApp (personal account) |
+|---|---|---|
+| Platform name | `whatsapp_cloud` | `whatsapp` |
+| Account | a business phone number in Meta's Cloud API | your own WhatsApp account, linked like WhatsApp Web |
+| Runs | inside the gateway; Meta calls a webhook | a bridge process on your machine |
+
+## WhatsApp Business (Cloud API)
+
+### What you need
+
+From a Meta developer app with the WhatsApp product: a **permanent access token**, the **phone
+number id**, the app's **app secret** (to check that webhook calls really come from Meta) and a
+**verify token** of your choice for the webhook handshake.
+
+### Setting it up
+
+```bash
+indus gateway setup whatsapp_cloud
+```
+
+or set `WHATSAPP_CLOUD_ACCESS_TOKEN`, `WHATSAPP_CLOUD_PHONE_NUMBER_ID`, `WHATSAPP_CLOUD_APP_SECRET`
+and `WHATSAPP_CLOUD_VERIFY_TOKEN`. The gateway's webhook listener binds to loopback; put it behind
+your HTTPS reverse proxy or tunnel, then enter that public URL and your verify token in Meta's
+webhook settings and subscribe to `messages`. Without the app secret the gateway refuses to receive
+anything, since unsigned calls could come from anyone.
+
+### How it behaves
+
+- Text is converted to WhatsApp's formatting and split at 4,096 characters.
+- Approvals and questions use reply buttons (up to three choices) or a list (up to ten).
+- Meta only allows free-form replies within 24 hours of the person's last message; a send outside
+  that window is refused and not retried.
+
+## WhatsApp (personal account)
+
+The `whatsapp` platform runs a small bridge process (Node.js 24) that holds a WhatsApp Web session.
+It needs a WhatsApp Web provider module that you install yourself and name in
+`platforms.whatsapp.provider`; Indus Agent does not ship one. Then set
+`platforms.whatsapp.enabled: true` and start the gateway. Linking the phone goes through the
+provider module; until the account is linked the gateway reports the platform as not paired, and
+`indus gateway status` says so.
+
+Direct messages need pairing or an allow-list; in groups the bot answers only when mentioned,
+replied to or addressed by one of its `mention_patterns`. A phone number and its WhatsApp alias
+count as one person.
diff --git a/docs/user/messaging/yuanbao.md b/docs/user/messaging/yuanbao.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9365d19
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/user/messaging/yuanbao.md
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# Yuanbao
+
+Indus Agent can work as a bot on Tencent Yuanbao.
+
+## What you need
+
+A Yuanbao bot's **App ID** and **App Secret**.
+
+## Setting it up
+
+```bash
+indus gateway setup yuanbao
+```
+
+or set `YUANBAO_APP_ID` and `YUANBAO_APP_SECRET`, then `indus gateway start`. The gateway keeps one
+signed WebSocket to Yuanbao, so nothing has to be public.
+
+## How it behaves
+
+- If another connection takes the bot over, the gateway stops using it and says so.
+- With the `yuanbao` toolset turned on, the agent gets Yuanbao's own tools as well.
diff --git a/docs/user/reference/cli.md b/docs/user/reference/cli.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ee3c44c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/user/reference/cli.md
@@ -0,0 +1,3380 @@
+<!-- Generated by scripts/docs/gen_reference.py. Do not edit: run the script. -->
+
+# Command line
+
+Every `indus` command with its arguments, options and subcommands.
+
+Every command also accepts `--help`, which prints the same text in the terminal.
+
+## indus
+
+Indus Agent: a terminal agent that can run commands, edit files and search the web.
+
+Run `indus` with no command to start a chat.
+
+```text
+indus [OPTIONS] [COMMAND] [ARGS]...
+```
+
+| Option | Value | Default | What it does |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `-V, --version` | flag |  | Show the version and how Indus Agent was installed. |
+| `-p, --profile` | TEXT |  | Run against the named profile (works in any position). |
+| `-z, --oneshot` | TEXT |  | Answer one prompt and print only the final reply (for scripts). |
+| `--usage-file` | TEXT |  | With -z: write a JSON usage report to PATH, even when the run fails. |
+| `-m, --model` | TEXT |  | Model for this run. |
+| `--provider` | TEXT |  | Provider for this run. |
+| `--reasoning` | TEXT |  | Reasoning effort: none, minimal, low, medium, high, xhigh, max or ultra. |
+| `-t, --toolsets` | TEXT |  | Comma-separated toolsets to enable. |
+| `-r, --resume` | TEXT |  | Resume a session by id or title; 'latest' picks the newest one here. |
+| `-c, --continue` | TEXT |  | Continue the session called NAME, or the newest one when no name is given. |
+| `--in` | TEXT |  | Work in DIR: change into it first and keep the session there. |
+| `--no-restore-cwd` | flag |  | Stay in the current directory when resuming. |
+| `-s, --skills` | TEXT (repeatable) |  | Skills to preload (repeat the flag or separate with commas). |
+| `-w, --worktree` | TEXT |  | Start the session in a new git worktree of this repository (named NAME). |
+| `--checkpoints` | flag |  | Snapshot the working folder before file changes (/rollback restores). |
+| `--yolo` | flag |  | Run risky commands without asking. |
+| `--accept-hooks` | flag |  | Run the configured shell hooks without asking about new ones first. |
+| `--pass-session-id` | flag |  | Tell the model its session id. |
+| `--ignore-user-config` | flag |  | Use built-in settings instead of config.yaml (.env still loads). |
+| `--ignore-rules` | flag |  | Skip project rules files, memory and preloaded skills. |
+| `--safe-mode` | flag |  | Troubleshoot with every customisation off (implies both --ignore flags). |
+| `--tui / --cli` | flag |  | Pick the full-screen interface or the classic prompt. |
+| `--local` | flag |  | Run the agent in this terminal instead of the profile's gateway daemon. |
+
